<BaseLayout title="About — Yui Taniyama" lang="en" translationHref="/ja/about/">
	<div class="prose">
		<h1>About</h1>
		<p>
			I'm a product designer with a background that started outside tech. For ten years I designed and helped
			bring over 1,200 products to market in fashion, before moving into digital product design.
		</p>
		<p>The materials changed, but the process didn't: research, sketch, prototype, refine, repeat.</p>
		<p>
			Most recently, I worked on hubstep, a CRM that grew from a direct-mail tool into a sales platform. I
			joined partway through its development, translated real-world feedback into UI/UX improvements, and
			later took on the Design System and product communication as the team's sole designer.
		</p>
		<p>
			Before that, as a UI/UX design intern at Freedom Tax Japan, I contributed competitive research, design
			exploration, and usability testing to a B2C redesign — working closely with a senior designer and the
			founder.
		</p>
		<p>I like being close to the people who use what I design, and close to the people I design it with.</p>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
